  attachedPhoto: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9bf918ecddb954a4db8c2f3a9837a18c, type: 3}
  logText: The capsule containing this specimen has detailed information about their
    physiology.\n\nTheir species name can be translated to Povann. They were an advanced
    underwater civilization that lived all over the oceans of the planet.\nThey have
    two long tentacle legs with fins for movement, as well as two smaller ones that
    they use like arms.\nThe tip of the small ones has many tiny fingers, comparable
    to the tentacles of a jellyfish.\nThere is a mouth at the bottom, used mainly
    for eating, and another one on the side of their body, used exclusively to communicate.\nThe
    Povann have a set of grills at the top of their heads and one large eye on each
    side.\nInterior scans of their organs show two hearts, each helping pump blood
    to one of their long legs.\nThe brain rests at the bottom of their body, between
    the mouths and the hearts.\nThey have a simple, hardened skeleton used to protect
    their vital organs, accompanied by cartilage covering most of the body.\n\nI
    should take all this information back to the ship for further investigation.
    Although I wish I could take the body with me.
  orderFound: 0
  read: 1
